You may view, read, inspect, and study the Source Code of the Software in its entirety for educational, academic, research, and personal security-audit purposes. This grant is explicitly and strictly limited to the visual consumption of the Source Code by natural human beings using standard text editors, integrated development environments (IDEs), or code-viewing applications. You may use standard code-analysis tools (such as linters, static analysis tools, code browsers, and syntax highlighters) to examine the structure, logic, architecture, and design of the Software, provided that:

(a) Such analysis is conducted solely for Your own understanding and intellectual development;

(b) Such analysis is not used to circumvent, defeat, or bypass any restriction or prohibition of this License;

(c) Such analysis does not result in the creation, distribution, or use of any Derivative Work;

(d) Such analysis does not reveal, expose, or publish any trade secrets, confidential information, or proprietary algorithms of the Licensor;

(e) You do not store, persist, or retain any analysis results, summaries, or extracted information except as strictly necessary for Your immediate review; and

(f) You do not share, publish, or disseminate any analysis results, findings, or observations with any third party, except as expressly permitted under Section 2.3.

### 2.2. Personal, Non-Commercial Compilation — Persönliche, Nicht-Kommerzielle Kompilierung

You may compile the Source Code into Binary form (Object Code) on a single computer owned or controlled by You for the sole and exclusive purpose of running the Software for Your own personal, private, non-commercial use. You may run the compiled Binary only if:

(a) It is compiled from the original, unmodified Source Code as provided by the Licensor, without any changes, additions, deletions, or alterations whatsoever;

(b) It is used on a single computer that is physically located at Your primary residence or place of study and is not accessible to any other person or entity;

(c) It is never accessed, used, shared, transmitted, or made available to any other person or entity, whether by network, file-sharing, physical transfer, or any other means;

(d) It is used exclusively for non-commercial purposes, as defined in Section 1.6;

(e) It is not used in any business, enterprise, organization, government agency, or any other entity;

(f) You do not create, store, or retain more than one (1) compiled Binary at any time;

(g) You do not use any automated build tools, continuous integration systems, or cloud-based compilation services to compile the Software;

(h) You maintain all Attribution Notices intact and unaltered in the compiled Binary;

(i) You do not remove, obscure, or disable any Technical Protection Measures embedded in the Source Code or Binary; and

(j) You are the sole user and operator of the compiled Binary.

### 2.3. Internal Security Research — Interne Sicherheitsforschung

You may analyze the Software for security vulnerabilities, bugs, defects, weaknesses, or other issues (collectively, "**Vulnerabilities**"), provided that:

(a) Such analysis is conducted solely for Your own personal and internal security research;

(b) Such analysis does not involve any automated or semi-automated vulnerability scanning, fuzzing, penetration testing, or other intensive analysis techniques that could disrupt, degrade, or harm the Software, its users, or its underlying systems;

(c) You do not exploit, weaponize, monetize, commercialize, or otherwise use any Vulnerability for any purpose other than private research;

(d) You do not publish, disclose, announce, publicize, or disseminate any information about any Vulnerability to any third party, including but not limited to security forums, mailing lists, blogs, social media, public databases, or any other public or private forum;

(e) Any Vulnerability discovered must be reported privately and confidentially to the Licensor through a designated secure channel (as specified on the Licensor's official website) within seventy-two (72) hours of discovery;

(f) The Vulnerability report shall be considered the confidential information and trade secret of the Licensor and shall not be shared with any third party;

(g) You shall not claim, assert, or imply any ownership, credit, or rights over any Vulnerability or its discovery;

(h) You shall not use any Vulnerability to harm, disrupt, compromise, or damage the Licensor, the Software, its users, or any third party;

(i) You shall not disclose any details of the Vulnerability to the Licensor's competitors, adversaries, or any other party; and

(j) You shall cooperate fully with the Licensor in investigating and remediating any Vulnerability reported hereunder.

### 2.4. Referential Citation — Referenzielle Zitation

You may cite the Software in academic papers, articles, dissertations, books, or other scholarly works for the purpose of scholarly critique, educational reference, or academic analysis, provided:

(a) You include the complete and accurate Attribution Notice as specified by the Licensor;

(b) You do not imply, explicitly or implicitly, any affiliation with, endorsement by, sponsorship by, or approval of the Licensor;

